<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What happened</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">UnitedHealth reported an 88.4% third-q=
uarter medical-care ratio, versus 89.9% one year earlier, including $610 mill=
ion of favorable reserve development. UnitedHealthcare=E2=80=99s operating ma=
rgin rose to 3.3% from 2.1%, reflecting benefit changes, pricing and medical-=
cost management. Medicare Advantage enrollment, however, contracted by 935,00=
0 members from year-end 2025. (UnitedHealth Group, <em>Third Quarter 2026 Res=
ults</em>, October 13, 2026.) (<a href=3D"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/=
data/731766/000073176626000255/earningsrelease3q26unh.htm" style=3D"color:#1a=
5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">sec.gov</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Optum Health revenue declined 10% year=
 over year because it reduced value-based-care membership in markets where it=
 lacked sufficient scale, while operating margin improved to 3.2% from 0.2%. =
Optum Insight revenue grew 3%, and operating earnings increased to $1.28 bill=
ion from $920 million, which management attributed to product enhancements an=
d operating efficiencies. (<a href=3D"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data=
/731766/000073176626000255/earningsrelease3q26unh.htm" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a=
;text-decoration:underline;">sec.gov</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Implication</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The results resolve an important opera=
ting question: UnitedHealth=E2=80=99s retrenchment is producing margin recove=
ry, but through narrower participation and greater local density=E2=80=94not =
broad membership growth. Competitors should expect continued discipline in MA=
 benefit design and provider contracting during the current enrollment cycle.=
</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">For provider groups, the Optum Health =
result reinforces that value-based-care capital will concentrate in markets w=
here an operator can align sufficient attributed lives, clinical capacity and=
 pharmacy or specialty services. For health-technology vendors, the evidence =
is stronger for demand tied to cost takeout, payment accuracy and clinician p=
roductivity than for indiscriminate expansion of risk-bearing care platforms.=
</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Whether 2027 enrollment stabilizes wit=
hout reversing the margin gains, and whether Optum resumes value-based-care g=
rowth only in markets where UnitedHealthcare or external payer volume provide=
s adequate density.</p>
<hr style=3D"border:0;border-top:1px solid #d5dde3;margin:18px 0;"/>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-3" name=3D"story-3" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>3. Humana retains clinic control =
while transferring more capital risk</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What happened</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Humana announced on October 13 that Bl=
ackRock=E2=80=99s HPS Investment Partners will acquire Welsh Carson=E2=80=99s=
 approximately $2.8 billion interest in joint ventures holding nearly 150 Cen=
terWell Senior Primary Care clinics. BlackRock will own a majority interest; =
CenterWell will retain a minority stake and continue managing all clinics. Th=
e venture expects to fund existing operations, new clinics and acquisitions o=
ver the next two years. (<a href=3D"https://humana.gcs-web.com/news-releases/=
news-release-details/humana-announces-new-strategic-joint-venture-blackrock-m=
anage" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">humana.gcs-web.com<=
/a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Unlike the legacy structure, the new v=
enture has no put option requiring Humana to repurchase the investor=E2=80=99=
s position. CenterWell may elect to purchase clinics beginning in 2028; if cl=
inics remain in 2033, BlackRock may initiate a sale process subject to Center=
Well=E2=80=99s first-offer right.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Implication</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Humana is separating operational contr=
ol from asset ownership. It preserves the clinical platform supporting MA car=
e management and risk economics while lowering balance-sheet liabilities and =
the cost of expansion capital. That makes continued clinic growth more feasib=
le following Humana=E2=80=99s Stars recovery without committing future qualit=
y-bonus revenue to real-estate and clinic-development obligations.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The trade-off is longer-term ownership=
 uncertainty. Humana retains management and optionality, but eventual purchas=
e or sale decisions could affect where care-delivery economics ultimately acc=
rue.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The amount and deployment of BlackRock=
=E2=80=99s additional capital, particularly whether growth favors de novo cli=
nics or acquisitions in markets aligned with Humana=E2=80=99s strongest MA co=
ntracts.</p>
<hr style=3D"border:0;border-top:1px solid #d5dde3;margin:18px 0;"/>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-4" name=3D"story-4" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>4. Alignment turns its Stars loss=
 into a regulatory-methodology challenge</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What happened</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Alignment filed suit on October 9 chal=
lenging its 2027 Star Ratings, after its California HMO contract=E2=80=94serv=
ing approximately 75% of company membership=E2=80=94fell from four stars to 3=
.5 stars. The complaint argues that CMS continued using measures not properly=
 adopted through notice-and-comment regulation, drawing on the earlier Clover=
 decision. (Alignment Healthcare, Form 8-K, October 8, 2026; Healthcare Dive,=
 <em>Alignment sues CMS over 2027 Medicare Advantage star ratings crash</em>,=
 October 13, 2026.) (<a href=3D"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/18324=
66/000162828026065470/alhc-20261008.htm?utm_source=3Dopenai" style=3D"color:#=
1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">sec.gov</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Implication</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Last week=E2=80=99s Stars divergence i=
s no longer solely a quality-execution issue; for affected contracts, it now =
includes legal option value. A successful expedited challenge could restore b=
onus economics, but no recalculation has occurred and Alignment must still ad=
dress the underlying HOS and Part D performance weaknesses it identified.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Plans facing disputed methodology need=
 parallel 2028 scenarios rather than assuming displayed ratings are either fu=
lly final or likely to be overturned. Reliable public timing for a merits dec=
ision was unavailable as of October 19.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Whether the court accelerates review b=
efore 2028 bid development and whether additional carriers challenge the same=
 measures.</p>
